---
import Frame from '../components/PageFrame.astro';
import { products } from '../data/site';
const items = [
  {
    title: 'Three products, one clear system',
    body: 'Follow a request, find the guidance behind it, and inspect the resulting picture of work.',
    href: '/platform/',
  },
  {
    title: 'A better way to coordinate work',
    body: 'Clear stages and named roles make the next decision easier to understand.',
    href: '/products/workflows/',
  },
  {
    title: 'Clarity for Malaysian SMEs',
    body: 'A practical concept for small teams: useful information, considered interfaces and fewer ambiguous actions.',
    href: '/about/',
  },
];
---

<Frame label="Home" items={items}>
  <section class="container section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">THREE PERSPECTIVES ON EVERYDAY WORK</p>
      <h2>A path. A source. A clearer picture.</h2>
      <p>
        Processes, documentation and reporting make more sense together. Explore
        one part of the story at a time through three working, browser-only
        demonstrations.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="product-grid">
      {products.map((p) => (
        <article class="product-card">
          <span class="product-symbol" aria-hidden="true">
            {p.symbol}
          </span>
          <h3>{p.name}</h3>
          <p>{p.description}</p>
          <a class="text-link" href={p.link}>
            Explore {p.name} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="dark-section">
    <div class="container split-section">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A CONSIDERED WAY TO BUILD</p>
        <h2>Make the important things visible.</h2>
        <p>
          Start with the question a person needs to answer. Put the next action
          within reach. Explain its consequence. Then make the details work with
          a keyboard, on a narrow screen, and without relying on colour alone.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/experience/">
          Explore the experience principles →
        </a>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>What this concept actually demonstrates</h3>
        <p>
          Original interface design, static Astro pages, local interactions,
          transparent sample data and accessible alternatives. No connected AI,
          automated business actions or fictional customers.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/technology/">
          See how the site works →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container section split-section">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">BEFORE THE TOOL, THE QUESTION</p>
      <h2>A smaller starting point can be a better one.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="reading">
      <p>
        If a request keeps getting lost, start by mapping its stages. If an
        answer is hard to find, make the source easier to inspect. If a chart
        feels convincing, ask whether its numbers support a decision.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our original field notes turn those questions into practical examples
        you can use beyond this fictional product.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/journal/">
        Read the journal →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Frame>
